  <table class="files-touched pl-files">
    <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Status</th><th>Module</th><th>Lines</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">config</span> e2e/package.json, package-lock.json, playwright.config.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">A private package with one pinned dependency, @playwright/test 1.63.0. Headless, 1280 by 800, one worker, bundled Chromium with the installed Edge as the fallback.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>e2e</td><td>+150</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> e2e/support/engine.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">Starts a real engine per test with a temporary data folder, reads the page address, generates the seed-2026 league, and reads the match records.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>harness</td><td>+160</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> e2e/tests/charter-scenario.spec.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">The twelve manager steps against the live engine, one screenshot and one checkpoint per step; step 12 reads the headless event stream for the AI change.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>e2e</td><td>+260</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> pitch, match-day, lineup-tactics, reports-recovery specs</summary><div class="pl-card">Every interactive viewer behaviour, bound to roles, names, and the page's read-only hook rather than to CSS classes.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>e2e</td><td>+700</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> e2e/tests/observability.spec.mjs</summary><div class="pl-card">A browser-driven match writes the event stream by the first stoppage and the statistics record within 2 seconds of full time.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>e2e</td><td>+110</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">test</span> licenses.rs, docs.rs</summary><div class="pl-card">License audit over the Rust and npm trees (no GPL or AGPL-only package); the document set exists and the command-line reference covers every flag.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>rust tests</td><td>+270</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-new"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> tutorial, how-to, cli and data-file reference, explanation, suite README</summary><div class="pl-card">The five planned documents at their target paths, plus the map from every viewer behaviour to its test or human check.</div></details></td><td>new</td><td>docs</td><td>+910</td></tr>
      <tr class="is-modified"><td><details><summary><span class="pl-chip">docs</span> README.md, content/README.md, .gitignore</summary><div class="pl-card">README links the documents and the suite; the content folder points at the moved reference; the suite's output folders are ignored.</div></details></td><td>modified</td><td>root</td><td>+47 / -212</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <div class="pl-risks">
    <aside class="callout callout-warn"><strong>A late performance miss on the complete engine.</strong> The last build ran 390 ms per match; later slices add work per tick. A miss stops the slice and returns the tick rate to the product owner.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Markup the suite binds to is still unwritten.</strong> Specs use roles, names, and the page hook, and each is written after its behaviour is verified.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>Headless frame timing.</strong> The page's own counter is the assertion; the headed run and the in-app browser drive are the fallbacks.</aside>
    <aside class="callout callout-info"><strong>An unowned record.</strong> The page's own session record has no owning slice; it sits outside this slice's criteria and is recorded so it is not lost.</aside>
  </div>

  <details class="pl-revs"><summary>0 prior revisions</summary><ul></ul></details>

